<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="93592449-8fa8-5030-8979-8ed50df91934" activityNameId="49303ad5-6dee-517d-b16f-f8f4f7891756" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Zinc coating, pieces</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Zinc coating, pieces
This module is applicable, if batch zinc coating of semifinished steel products, that's shape doesn't change anymore, has to be balanced. Data given per tonne of coated product had to be transformed dividing it by the mean surface area of 60 m2/t.  For the chemicals and the zinc, 100 km of 32t lorry transport were balanced. The softened industrial water is assumed to be produced at the coating plant. The coating layer is 65um thick, if the surface is coated on both sides and 130 um thick, if coating is done on one side only. Due to the fact, that data are given per square meter and not per kg, the energy inventoried for heavy pieces is to low and for light pieces to high. If the data would have been given per kg, the error would have been the contrary.;
Synonyms: hot dip coating, galvanising; 
UUID: 887baada-b40f-39b4-b4f1-63f03606e790
Includes the process steps degreasing, pickling, fluxing, galvanising (melt zinc coating) and finishing. Does not include the fabricates being coated.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Average technique for EU. 
Time period: undefined
Production volume: 5 million tonnes in 1997
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: see technology
Uncertainty adjustments: The fact that no data were available about the percentage of companies represented by the study citated is considered in the uncertainties.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_887baada-b40f-39b4-b4f1-63f03606e790.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
